{"kind":"request","text":"Security R16 (one-channel audit 1e8ef5d5, disposition D13): an application can publish any path.\n\nFound at main c40492ee. `publish-file` from any application scope of a room sends a path and a text to the destination, and the destination commits it (packages/platform/src/destination.ts:2592-2595). The fold publication note allows any application scope to write any path (notes/2026-10-13-fold-publication.md, section 6). The only path check refuses control characters, empty segments, `.` and `..` and `.git` (packages/bytes/src/edit-path.ts:11-15). So an installed application can write `.github/workflows/*`, which a GitHub-hosted room would run with its secrets, and the repository files that the room's rules read as control files. A change lane would judge the same edit under the rules extents; a publication is not judged that way.\n\nWork:\n1. Reserved paths. No application publication writes `.github/` or any path that the room's rules or destination read as control (for example the rules extent files). List every reserved path in the head report, with where each is read.\n2. Declared prefixes. An application package declares the path prefixes it publishes under. The host checks the declaration at install against the reserved paths and the room's rules extents, and refuses an install that claims a reserved path.\n3. Each publication. A publication outside the application's declared prefixes, or inside a reserved path, is refused, and the refusal is recorded with a reason. For new rooms, put the judged check in a new destination version. Do not change pinned destination rules in place: replay of existing rooms must stay unchanged (the same rule as the 3.12 ruling 9d8f12a7). For rooms already pinned to an older destination, the host's publication step refuses a reserved or undeclared path, and the operation's outcome entry records the refusal.\n4. Compatibility. Existing packages keep working: the lending library's shelf pages and the Grow package publish under prefixes that their next release declares. For a package with no declaration, state the default prefix and show that the hosted demos keep publishing after the redeploy.\n5. Documentation: the fold publication note's section 6 and docs/application-views.md or the package docs say what an application can write.\n\nWitnesses:\n- A publication to `.github/workflows/x.yml` is refused with its reason, both under the new destination version and through the host step of an older pinned destination.\n- A publication to a rules extent file is refused the same way.\n- A publication inside the declared prefix is accepted and committed.\n- An install whose package claims a reserved prefix is refused.\n- The lending library's shelf pages still publish. Replay of an existing room's journal is unchanged.\n\nPlace in the security order: right after R8 (8ced57e3), before R5. The archive items keep priority (F3 8fda2549, step 6 7b19837c). The planner deploys after review: artroom-scope, dap-grow and dap-lending; the head report lists each new setting and redeploy step.","body":{"conditions":"Reserved paths, declared publication prefixes checked at install and at each publication, a new destination version for new rooms and a recorded host refusal for pinned ones, no change to pinned rules, existing demos keep publishing. Checker review on every head; one gate at the final head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment. Security order: right after R8, before R5.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}